WEBVTT

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:03.820
You've got your sights set on taking your business global and reaching more

00:00:03.820 --> 00:00:05.808
customers, but don't know where to start.

00:00:05.808 --> 00:00:08.080
In this step, we'll cover the things you

00:00:08.080 --> 00:00:11.480
should consider when deciding where and what to sell in Amazon's global

00:00:11.480 --> 00:00:12.000
marketplaces.

00:00:12.000 --> 00:00:16.160
First, do some research on your potential customers.

00:00:16.160 --> 00:00:17.200
Amazon has

00:00:17.200 --> 00:00:21.600
marketplaces in North America, Europe, and Asia, each with different customer

00:00:21.600 --> 00:00:23.208
preferences, cultures, and languages.

00:00:23.208 --> 00:00:25.620
It's important to understand what those

00:00:25.620 --> 00:00:30.449
customers need and how you can tailor your product to meet those needs.

00:00:30.449 --> 00:00:30.820
Next,

00:00:30.820 --> 00:00:31.989
decide what to sell.

00:00:31.989 --> 00:00:34.620
This includes making sure your product works in that

00:00:34.620 --> 00:00:39.800
country and that you're compliant with all local taxes, regulations, and laws.

00:00:39.800 --> 00:00:44.900
Amazon has services that can help manage those details for you, making the global

00:00:44.900 --> 00:00:46.736
selling journey that much easier.

00:00:46.736 --> 00:00:50.040
With a little thought and help from Amazon global

00:00:50.040 --> 00:00:55.640
selling, you can be open for business all over the world in no time.
